# LAMMPS examples/granregion/in.granregion.box with the container's walls given the pair
# style (gran/hooke, a tangential dashpot without spring, as the module uses one tangential
# model for both), energies summed in the thermo output, and the (1, 1, 1) rotation axis
# normalized: LAMMPS (22 Jul 2025, region.cpp set_velocity) multiplies the angular rate by the
# axis as given for the wall velocity while it rotates the geometry about the unit axis, so an
# unnormalized axis makes the walls push sqrt(3) times too fast. Run with
#   lmp -in in.granregion.box
units		lj
atom_style      sphere
boundary        f f f
dimension	3
comm_modify     vel yes
region          box block -11 11 -11 11 -11 11 units box
create_box      2 box
Created orthogonal box = (-11 -11 -11) to (11 11 11)
  1 by 1 by 1 MPI processor grid
pair_style	hybrid gran/hooke 4000.0 NULL 100.0 NULL 0.5 1
pair_coeff	* * gran/hooke
region          container block -6 6 -6 6 -6 6 units box
fix		container all wall/gran/region hooke 4000.0 NULL 100.0 NULL 0.5 1 region container
neighbor	0.3 bin
neigh_modify	delay 0 every 1 check yes
fix             2 all nve/sphere
fix		3 all gravity 1.0 vector 0 0 -1
region          slab block -2 2 -2 2 -2 2 units box
fix             ins all pour 100 2 4767548 vol 0.4 10 diam one 1.0 region slab ignore
timestep	0.005
compute         kea all ke/atom
compute         ke all reduce sum c_kea
compute         erot all erotate/sphere
thermo		100
thermo_style	custom step atoms c_ke c_erot
thermo_modify   norm no lost warn
run	        5000
